om2
note tools/gen/protocol/genstats.om -- reference statistics of the GEN decision rule (aien-spark/omega#476,
note docs/one_layer/GEN_PROTOCOL_V1.md section 9). Writes tests/one_layer/generalization/stats_vectors.tsv,
note the test vectors the GEN reducer (tools/gen/reducer, omega#477) must reproduce. Pure OM-2 port of
note tools/gen/protocol/genstats.c; the C file stays as the protocol-pinned reference (protocol.json pins).
note
note   genstats wilson <k> <n> <95|90>             "p lo hi"
note   genstats mcnemar1 <b> <c>                   "p_num p_den p": exact one-sided McNemar,
note                                               P(Bin(b+c, 1/2) >= b) = p_num / p_den, p_den = 2^(b+c)
note   genstats newcombe <a> <b> <c> <d> <95|90> [8|10]
note                                               "theta lo hi": Newcombe (1998, Stat Med 17:2635) paired
note                                               interval for p1 - p2, method 10 (default) or 8
note   genstats verdict <valid 0|1> <A> <B> <C> <D>  the full decision from four 0/1 strings (n = 60 only)
note   genstats lenmatch <target>:<suffix>...      length-matched ablation classes (section 10)
note   genstats vectors                            print the whole stats_vectors.tsv
note   genstats selftest                           Newcombe Table III, McNemar tail identity, Wilson nesting
note Exact integer arithmetic for McNemar (128-bit as two ulong words, b + c <= 120); IEEE binary64 elsewhere,
note operation for operation as the C reference compiles (gcc -O2 on AArch64 fuses the four products of the
note Newcombe variance terms and the phi numerator into FMADD/FMSUB/FNMSUB; this port writes those as fma).
note Reals are printed as glibc printf %.Nf does: the exact binary value rounded half to even.
note Deterministic: no clock, no randomness, no environment.

const GS_Z95 f64 1.959963984540054
const GS_Z90 f64 1.644853626951472

text gs_usage "usage: genstats wilson <k> <n> <95|90> | mcnemar1 <b> <c> | newcombe <a> <b> <c> <d> <95|90> [8|10] | verdict <valid> <A> <B> <C> <D> | lenmatch <target>:<suffix>... | vectors | selftest\n"
